 "about": "Re-captured on 2.1.310 (2026-10-25): the same events, pairing and denied-call batches. Claude Code 2.1.280 hook payloads captured 2026-10-24 by a capture-only hook in headless claude -p runs (claude-sonnet-5) in a scratch git repo, for the foreign-edit warning (tasks/SPEC-FOREIGN-EDIT-WARNING.md). Trimmed to the fields the hook reads; session id, paths and transcript paths replaced. offset_s is seconds from SessionStart. parallel_and_background was captured before PostToolBatch was wired, so it has no batch events. Findings: Pre and Post pair by tool_use_id, and two parallel Bash calls overlap (Pre, Pre, Post, Post); a call denied by a permission rule or blocked by a PreToolUse hook gets no PostToolUse, but PostToolBatch fires after every batch, denied ones included; a failing command fires PostToolUseFailure with the same tool_use_id; a background Bash fires PostToolUse at launch with backgroundTaskId; subagent calls share the parent session_id and add agent_id and agent_type, and their batches end with their own PostToolBatch.",
